meta {
  name: analyze a session's file calls (NDJSON stream)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/files/analyze
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "digest": "workspace: /tmp/demo\n#1 0.5s main run_command: echo hi > notes.txt",
    "provider": "ollama",
    "model": "qwen2.5:7b",
    "lang": "en"
  }
}

docs {
  Opt-in one-shot LLM reading of the files tab's digest (one line per file call), on the provider and model named in the body, local providers included and the built-in model refused. Streamed as NDJSON ({meta:{provider,model,address}}, {delta}..., {done}|{error}). Reasoning is off; an empty answer is an error with a fixed sentence, not a done. The digest is never logged. 400 blank digest, missing pair or built-in model; 413 oversize; 503 pair cannot be built (card 604).
  
  Body: FilesAnalyzeBody(String digest, String provider, String model, String lang): digest required, max 60000 chars; provider and model required; lang en | de.
  
  CAUTION: Spends the key of the picked provider on every call, unless that provider is local.
  
  Fence: host+origin+json. Loopback fence plus Origin check, and the request must carry Content-Type: application/json — anything else is 415.
  
  Writes state: no
}
